! conclusion: Pin the defect (ONE figure on the page) and supply the evidence as an observed/expected contrast (expected per-PBASE-type breakouts), making the report self-serve — the agent located the missing link and fixed it with no clarifying dialogue.

  + IF:
    The operator reports a defect in a rendered artefact the agent can inspect.

  + HOWEVER:
    A bare 'it looks wrong' costs reproduction round-trips; the operator's eye is the expensive instrument.

  + THEN:
    Pin the defect (ONE figure on the page) and supply the evidence as an observed/expected contrast (expected per-PBASE-type breakouts), making the report self-serve — the agent located the missing link and fixed it with no clarifying dialogue.

  + BECAUSE:
    This turn is another earned instance of the existing draft proposal (kimi-3, 2026-09-24, already earned from 12 turns). Cited rather than re-minted to avoid doubling the vocabulary. Variant worth noting on the proposal: here the evidence is an observed/expected contrast rather than a pasted passage — the expectation doubles as the acceptance test.
